  "notes": "A house-influenced contemporary-soul producer, 1998–2010; the band is \"64–103 straight; ballads 64–71 half-time\", and the straight half is the base: the stated ballad top of 71 fixes the straight complement at 72–103 exactly. Three drum deltas from a first-person account of the rig: \"**ASR-10 (early) → Logic Pro (current)**; the drums are borrowed and curated rather than synthesised from scratch — he documents using a drum library given to him by Dr. Dre\". So the kit is authored as a curated sample kit rather than a designed one — a swung 0.58 grid, a clap layered 1–4 ms behind the snare, and real ghost activity on `2e` and `4a`. The distinguishing delta is \"a house-derived bounce\": the hat runs continuous 16ths at a 0.5 fill density with open hats on both offbeats at 0.34, and the perc lanes are placed `offbeat`. Harmony is his stated method, quoted: he composes **chord-first** — \"I was just trying to give him some chords that would make him feel good about getting in the studio\" — so the four-chord m7/maj7 cycles carry the model, the triad share falls to 0.14, and the Wurlitzer/Rhodes lead is the timbre hint. \"Melodies written on the spot in the room with the singer\" is why the melody is authored conservatively around the changes. The bass follows the same house influence: \"sub-kick plus a played or synth bass on roots; house influence shows in the bass moving in 8ths on the up-tempos\", so `rhythm` is `offbeat_8ths` with repeated-root cells and no `bass808` block. ⚠ The bpm mode is INFERRED: the entry names no tempo inside its own 64–103 band — the one catalogue tempo it gives, Brandy \"Full Moon\" at 106, sits above it — so 95 is this author's centre of gravity, not a reading. ⚠ Confidence is medium — the research rates it high-medium on gear, method and workflow, all first-person — and every velocity and density number is INFERRED. ⚠ `session.keys` is INFERRED: the entry's Keys line gives \"minor-mode with maj7 colour\" and enumerates no tonic, so the values here and their weights are this author's reading of that line.",
